 This criterion follows directly if you look at the sequence of unfoldings."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we have a solution: for each directed edge in a tree compute a set of depths to the leaves by a 2-way tree DP (actually, it must be computed only if its size is at most 1). Afterwards for each vertex check the root criterion."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, there is an idea which makes the solution simpler: the midpoint of the diameter of the given tree is always an appropriate root. Given this, we should only run a standard tree DP which checks if all leaves in a subtree have the same depth."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here is the outline of a proof: in the path from the first paragraph select the leftmost and the rightmost possible root, now look through all possible distances from left root to the left leaf and from the right root to the right leaf. There are several configurations which are easy to check manually."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"765F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/765/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"765F - Souvenirs"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We will answer queries offline, moving right endpoint to the right and storing the answer for each left endpoint in a segment tree. The tree will support two operations: set minimum on a segment and get a value in the point. More, we assume that among two elements "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" in our array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and solve the problem twice — for the original array and for the reversed one."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider one step of moving the right endpoint and adding new element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". We find the first element to the left of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" which is not less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"; denote it with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Obviously, now the answer for all left endpoints in range [0, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Now we find some "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"ki